From e0a99816ec0fa3a1f01aebf20d1a161e51b0ddd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:11:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): let capped queued cards escape held machine pins
 [daveey]

A held draining worker cannot claim its machine-pinned ready cards. The
move cap previously stranded portable work there after three moves.
Extend the existing queued dead-pin rescue with affirmative boolean hold
evidence from the same fresh registry read. Audit held_pin separately,
keep counting the rescue, and retain all target, ping-pong and source guards.
No source hold, scaler, or max_moves configuration is changed.

Proof: RED three regression cases fail with move_limit; GREEN 426 tests
in 22 move/source/capability files and 806 tests in 26 other consumer files.
Five condition mutants killed, including running/multi-pin/malformed-hold
controls. Real registry cache expiry and failed-refresh TTL tested.
scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks ok, no health findings.

Hermes-Card: t_eeeeee000000003e
